    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d610">

                <pb facs="1066" n="932" xml:id="pg932"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source"> J. C. S. Files</note>
                <head>No. 610<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Representatives of the
                        British Chiefs of Staff</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]<anchor n="1" xml:id="d610-f1"/></seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                        <lb/> C. C. S. 877/1</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-06-30">30 June 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Basic Objectives, Strategy, and Policies</hi>
                </p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . .</p>
                <p>5. Subject to the above remarks<anchor n="2" xml:id="d610-f2"/> the British
                    Chiefs of Staff are in full agreement with the memorandum by the United States
                    Chiefs of Staff (C. C. S. 877),<anchor n="3" xml:id="d610-f3"/>. …</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d610-f1" n="1" xml:id="d610-f1-content">
                <p>For the full text of this memorandum, see <ref target="#d600">document No.
                        600</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d610-f2" n="2" xml:id="d610-f2-content">
                <p>None of the remarks referred to concerned paragraph 6 a of C. C. S. 877, quoted
                    in footnote 3, <hi rendition="#italic">infra.</hi>
                </p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d610-f3" n="3" xml:id="d610-f3-content">
                <p>Concerning the text of this memorandum, see <ref target="#d600">document No.
                        600</ref>, <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, footnote 1, and <ref
                        target="frus1945Berlinv02#d1263">document No. 1263, printed in vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">ii</hi>
                    </ref>. The passage here pertinent reads as follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“6. The following additional tasks will be undertaken in order to assist
                            in the execution of the over-all strategic concept:—</p>
                        <p>“<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>. Encourage Russian entry into the war
                            against Japan. Provide such aid to her war-making capacity as may be
                            necessary and practicable in connection therewith.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
